finding: Stage 1 does not preserve the explicit manual gate for all source-map mutations. `scripts/prepare-sourcemaps.ts` changed `sourcemaps:prepare` from validating and printing a Datadog command into immediately invoking `bunx --no-install datadog-ci sourcemaps upload` for each demo. Its only guards are a staging artifact, a caller-provided hostname, and `DD_API_KEY`; it does not require the workflow-dispatch opt-in or any separate upload confirmation. Thus a local invocation with credentials and those arguments uploads maps outside the manual gate, while prior/default local callers of `bun run sourcemaps:prepare [outDir]` now fail rather than prepare/display the plan. The workflow's `if` conditions protect only workflow steps, not this now-mutating command. Evidence: compared `origin/main:scripts/prepare-sourcemaps.ts` (only `console.log(formatSourceMapUploadCommand(...))`) with the committed script; verified the committed spawn arguments invoke Datadog's `sourcemaps upload` command using the pinned installed CLI. No upload was performed.
